#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:47
msgid "Get the security overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:48
msgid "This site’s Overview as data, from the payload its Overview screen draws: the score and grade and what the one-click fixes would make them, the last 30 recorded days, open findings by severity with the snoozed ones counted apart, and how many are marked not applicable; each open and not-applicable finding with its area, points, status, first and last seen, snooze, whether the last audit could check it, and its fix (the protection that answers it, whether it is on and how a connection may apply it, or where the setting is); the last audit’s time and the checks it could not run; this week’s receipts and what the plugin costs a page view; safe mode, which pauses protections and never changes the score; and whether each way back in would work today. Fixed findings only with include_fixed. No evidence payloads."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:67
msgid "List this site’s incidents"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:68
msgid "Up to 20 stored incidents with confidence and evidence counts. Open incidents do not expire; handled history follows retention. No correlation work or response action runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:74
msgid "Get an incident’s timeline"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:75
msgid "Up to 100 evidence records after a stable evidence ID. Explicit time links, recorded account IDs, paths and bounded summaries; no credentials, full addresses or response handles. Does not prove malicious intent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:81
msgid "See which hardening switches are on"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:82
msgid "Saved control states and observation support, with each control’s group, how a connection may apply it (directly, after a person confirms, or never), whether it can be undone, whether it can work on this server and why not, what else already does its job, a failed undo, how far it reaches on a network, the strict transport and content policy settings in force, and what a watch window has seen. Omits control options, hidden login paths and undo handles; does not apply controls or probe the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:87
msgid "Get login protection settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:88
msgid "Login thresholds, enabled mechanisms and address-list counts; the comment, password reset and registration forms’ own limits and what each does when one is reached; the recommended limits; how this request’s client address was worked out; how many lockouts there are and how many are running; whether a session limit can be kept here; and how many accounts are signed in. No trusted address values, source addresses or unlock credentials."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:93
msgid "See two-factor and passkey rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:94
msgid "Site and effective two-factor/passkey role requirements, including the network minimum. Reading does not start anyone’s enrollment grace period."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:99
msgid "List this site’s users and roles"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:100
msgid "Up to 50 current-site members after a user ID, plus a bounded role inventory. No email addresses, login names, credentials or per-user private metadata."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:106
msgid "See when a user was last active"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:107
msgid "Up to 20 live sessions for one current-site member, defaulting to the caller. Session tokens, hashes, IP addresses and browser strings are never returned. On multisite these are account sessions shared across the network."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:113
msgid "List quarantined files"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:114
msgid "Metadata from matching ledger entries, newest first, up to 200 a page: original relative path, size, digest and availability. Pass before_id from a previous answer to read older entries. No file contents, storage paths, download links or undo tokens."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:120
msgid "Check background tasks are running"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:121
msgid "The current request’s bounded cron audit: unanswered third-party hooks and counts, and whether the schedule itself is being run (how far this plugin’s own hooks are overdue, and whether that counts as stalled). Hook arguments are never returned and no task runs. Unanswered does not mean malicious."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:126
msgid "Get one check’s result"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:127
msgid "One check’s explanation, risk guidance and last recorded status. Does not rerun the check or return its raw evidence payload."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:133
msgid "See which backup plugin is installed"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:134
msgid "Recognized active and inactive backup plugins. Host backups, backup age and restore testing remain unknown; plugin presence is not proof of a usable backup."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:139
msgid "Get this site’s own settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:140
msgid "How the site’s own email alerts are set, with recipients counted and never named, and how many were sent in the window the log keeps; the password policy; whether a security contact file is published and until when; whether usage data is shared; and what uninstalling removes. No addresses, contact details or reasons. Changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:151
msgid "List changes since a given time"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:152
msgid "This site’s own list of what changed since the time given, as its Overview lists what changed since a person last looked: up to eight, the ones worth leading with first, with whether there were more and whether the log no longer reaches back that far. Reading it moves nobody’s last visit."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:158
msgid "Get this site’s agent connections"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:159
msgid "Whether the MCP server is on; the paired credential (whether one is paired, since when, who holds it and what it may do); each application holding a grant, with its name, what it may do, who approved it and when, when it was last used and whether it is the hub; the hub connection’s host and when it was granted; the connection’s health; how many requests wait for a person; whether agent activity is recorded and the hourly limits on changes and plans; and whether unused application passwords are retired, a decoy credential is armed and when it was last used, and a decoy address is armed. No credential, token hint, decoy name, path or address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:173
msgid "List the network’s sites"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:174
msgid "On a network, for a super administrator: each site’s name and address, whether this plugin is installed there, whether its MCP server and read abilities are on and whether it is connected to the hub, and its last score, grade, open findings and audit time (0, empty and 0 until it has been audited), from the roll-up the Network screen reads. Pass next_cursor back as cursor for the next page; an empty one is the last. Changes nothing on any site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:180
msgid "Get this site’s Hub link"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:181
msgid "Whether this site sends its security events and a heartbeat to BetterShield Hub, signed: the public key the hub checks them against, the id the site signs as, and which kinds of events it sends. Off, the key and the id are empty: the link is off, or this is a copy at another address or a staging copy, or the site is not connected to hub.bettershield.ai. Pass the hub’s nonce (32 bytes, base64url) as challenge to get proof: the key’s Ed25519 signature, base64url, over five lines joined by a newline: “bettershield hub link proof v1”, https://hub.bettershield.ai, this site’s home URL without a trailing slash, the site id and the challenge. Empty without a challenge or while the link is off. Never the secret key."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:187
msgid "List this site’s lockouts"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:188
msgid "Up to 100 lockouts a page, newest first: each one’s form, the network it came from as a /24 or /64, when it started and ends, whether it is running and how many attempts set it off, with how many there are and how many are running. Pass next_cursor back as cursor for older ones; an empty one is the last page. No username, full address or way to lift one."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:194
msgid "Get this site’s software versions"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/ReadSurface.php:195
msgid "The WordPress and PHP versions, the active theme, how many plugins are installed and active, and how many updates WordPress already knows are waiting, with when it last looked. Also this plugin’s version, whether BetterShield Ultra is loaded and its version, on a network which site this is, and the address of this site’s dashboard. Counts and versions only: no plugin is named, and nothing is asked of WordPress.org."
msgstr ""

