msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:519
msgid "Security posture, activity and integrity for this site. Reading is always offered. Changing the site is offered only where the owner has turned that on, and a change is then either one the undo record can take back exactly or one a person has to allow first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:612
msgid "Get the security score"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:613
msgid "The security score, grade, and open findings for this site, each with a plain-language explanation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:690
msgid "Query activity"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:691
msgid "A bounded, paginated window over the activity log. Retention limits are applied silently and reported in the response."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:760
msgid "Get file check results"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:761
msgid "File integrity state against wordpress.org checksums: hashes and paths only, never file contents. The open changes, or with list set to expected the accepted ones; whether a check is running and how far it has got; and how many are accepted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:888
msgid "See what AI tools other plugins offer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:889
msgid "What agents can do on this site: every registered ability with its declared annotations, REST exposure and low-privilege reachability, and application-password holdings as counts and ages, never names."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:940
msgid "Get vulnerability state"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:941
msgid "Known vulnerabilities affecting what this site runs. States plainly when no data source is configured, since an empty answer is not a clean bill of health."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1011
msgid "Query agent activity"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1012
msgid "A bounded, paginated window over Abilities API invocations on this site, whoever registered the ability. Inputs are recorded as digests and never returned. Retention limits are applied silently and reported in the response."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1098
msgid "Check app passwords and stored keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1099
msgid "Which AI connector credentials this site holds, where each is stored, and how many plugins can read them. Never returns credential values or key hints."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1145
msgid "Get recovery readiness"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1146
msgid "Whether each way back in works today, and whether a change to how people sign in would be allowed now. Never returns the recovery link or a code."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1281
msgid "Suggest turning a protection on or off"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1282
msgid "Describes exactly what applying one protection would do to this site (or what taking one off would do, with action set to \"revert\"), and records the plan so a person can allow it. Changes nothing either way. When this connection may change the site, the answer carries the confirmation the act takes: show the plan to the person and act once they agree. Otherwise the plan is allowed from the dashboard. Taking a protection off always needs one of these plans: apply-hardening puts a reversible protection on by itself, and nothing takes one off by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1325
msgid "Suggest putting a file back"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1326
msgid "Describes what replacing one changed file with its published copy would do, including how much differs and the checksum it would be restored to. Changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1362
#: src/Rest/AgentWriteController.php:399
msgid "Put a file back"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1363
msgid "Puts the published copy of one changed file back, once, with the confirmation for the plan propose-file-restore returned. The file as it is now goes to quarantine first, the published copy is checked against its checksum before it is used, and the answer carries the handle revert-hardening takes to put the current file back. That way back is best effort, not guaranteed, which is why this waits for the person’s agreement."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1389
#: src/Rest/AgentWriteController.php:395
msgid "Apply a protection"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1390
msgid "Applies one protection. A reversible protection is applied directly and the answer carries the handle that puts it back. A protection that changes how people sign in is refused here and named a proposal: a connection a person has allowed to change the site gets the confirmation back with the plan and applies it once the person agrees in the conversation; callers outside the connected assistant use the dashboard to allow a plan."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1444
msgid "Undo a change"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1445
msgid "Restores what a change made through these abilities replaced, using the handle it returned. A plugin switched back on and a restored file put back are the safe direction and ask for nothing more. Taking a protection off is not the safe direction, whatever put it there: for that, ask propose-hardening with action \"revert\", show the person the plan, and send the confirmation it carries. A finding fix’s handle (scheduled events, a REST route, a folder, a plugin update or quarantine, an account change) takes its plan from propose-fix-undo the same way."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1484
msgid "Suggest switching a plugin off"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1485
msgid "Describes what switching one plugin off would do to this site, and records the plan so a person can allow it. Changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1510
msgid "Switch off a confirmed plugin"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1511
msgid "Switches off the plugin a person allowed, once, using the confirmation they minted. The prior state is recorded first, so it can be switched back on."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1549
msgid "Choose the action the site offers. Execution needs its proposal and single-use confirmation, with no replacement target."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1611
msgid "Choose one access action. Execution needs its proposal and single-use confirmation, with no replacement target."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1653
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2112
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2722
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2896
msgid "That confirmation belongs to a different change."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1665
#: src/Integrity/Restore.php:1031
msgid "That file change has already been dealt with."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1666
msgid "That incident already has this status."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1671
msgid "Accepts this file change, so it no longer appears among open changes. Does not edit the file. Undo reports the change again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1671
msgid "Marks this incident handled and stops collecting new evidence for it. Undo reopens it as acknowledged and resumes collection."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1671
msgid "Labels this incident acknowledged. Evidence collection continues and no protection changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1741
msgid "There is no such protection."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1747
msgid "A plan is for putting a protection on or for taking it off. Name one of those as the action, or leave it out to plan putting it on."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1755
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2456
msgid "This protection writes a rule block into a shared configuration file, which stays the site owner’s own switch. It is not described or applied through an ability."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1793
msgid "This protection is not offered on this installation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1824
msgid "Changes how people sign in. If it goes wrong, the way back in is the recovery link: this site verifies it daily, it must have been verified within the last day for the change to be allowed, and pressing the button on the page it opens puts the site in safe mode with every protection relaxed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1881
msgid "This protection is not on, so there is nothing here to take off."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1892
msgid "There is no record on this site of what this protection replaced, so taking it off stays the site owner’s own switch rather than something described or carried out here."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1909
msgid "Takes this protection off the site and puts back what the undo record kept from before it. Until it is put on again:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1923
msgid "Changes how people sign in: the way in goes back to the one WordPress ships. Anybody using the address or the gate this protection put in place will need the original one again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:1991
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2123
#: src/Abilities/WriteTriage.php:53
#: src/Integrity/Restore.php:1025
msgid "There is no such file change on record."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2033
msgid "Takes a copy of the file as it is now into quarantine before anything is written."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2034
msgid "Fetches the published copy for this exact version and checks it against the published checksum before it is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2035
msgid "Writes that copy over the file on disk, and records the prior state in the undo ledger first. That way back is best effort, not guaranteed, since the file, its path or the quarantined copy may have moved by the time it is asked for, which is why this change waits for a person."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2142
msgid "This file is not in the state the plan described, so the plan no longer describes it. Ask for the change again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2201
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2668
msgid "That change is not one these abilities made."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2236
msgid "The file as it was before the restore is back from quarantine, byte for byte."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2287
msgid "This names a plan, so it needs the confirmation a person minted for that plan. Send the confirmation, or leave the proposal out to apply a protection directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2301
msgid "Name the plan this confirmation was minted for, as proposal_id. Nothing was changed and the confirmation still stands."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2354
msgid "This protection is not applied through an ability."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: what the site says about this protection now.
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2373
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2543
#, php-format
msgid "This site has changed since that plan was made, so the plan no longer describes it: %s. Ask for the change again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2437
#: src/Abilities/Registrar.php:2448
msgid "Name the protection to apply."
