msgid "A hash naming a sign-in that is waiting on the second-factor screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:199
msgid "It is how that screen finds the sign-in it belongs to, without the sign-in itself being stored where a hash could open it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:200
msgid "until that sign-in finishes, or the next one replaces it"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:204
msgid "When a two-factor deadline started for this account on this site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:205
msgid "The clock starts when the policy first applies to the account, not when the account was made, so switching the policy on shuts nobody out the same day."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:206
msgid "until two-factor is set up on the account"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:210
msgid "That the password was below this site’s policy the last time it was seen."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:211
msgid "It is what asks for a new one, and there is nowhere else to read it from, because a stored password cannot be measured again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:212
msgid "until the password is changed to one that meets the policy"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:216
msgid "That the password was confirmed recently, and for which sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:217
msgid "An action that takes a protection off asks once, and then not again for a short while."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:218
#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:224
msgid "until the confirmation lapses, a few minutes later"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:222
msgid "That one of the account’s own passkeys confirmed it recently, and for which sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:223
msgid "An account that signs in by passkey alone confirms it is its holder this way before its passkeys change, and is then not asked again for a short while."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:228
msgid "The date this plugin last saw the account sign in."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:229
msgid "It is the input to the check that finds accounts with real permissions nobody is using any more."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:232
msgid "An account that reads as never used is one nobody is ever asked to close, so the date stays and the answer to the request says it stayed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:235
msgid "Which version’s release panel this account has dismissed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:236
msgid "So a panel that has been read is not shown again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:241
msgid "The REST routes and the network each of this account’s application passwords is held to, where a limit was set."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:242
msgid "So a request with one of those passwords outside its limit is refused."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:243
msgid "Until the limit is removed or the password is revoked."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:245
msgid "Erasing it would let the account’s application passwords reach everything again, from anywhere. It is a setting on a credential, and the answer to the request says it stayed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:250
msgid "A new email address for this account waiting for confirmation from that address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:251
msgid "So a change to where password resets go takes effect only once the new address confirms it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:252
msgid "Until the change is confirmed or canceled."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:256
msgid "Changes to how this account can be signed in to, with the time, a /24 or /64 network and the browser, waiting to be emailed to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:257
msgid "So changes made within a few minutes reach the account holder as one email."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:258
msgid "About ten minutes, until the email is sent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:262
msgid "When this account last looked at the overview screen on this site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:263
msgid "It is what tells a return from a refresh, so the overview can say what changed since the last one."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:268
msgid "Which stretch of time the overview screen treats as new for the sitting in progress."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:269
msgid "Held still while the screen is being read, or what changed empties on a refresh."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:274
msgid "The truncated network each open session was started from, and on a network which site it was started on and whether a passkey started it, written beside WordPress’s own record of that session."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:275
msgid "The sessions screen says where a session came from, and this is how it says a network rather than the address WordPress keeps there. On a network, a site holds a session started on another site to its own sign-in rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:276
msgid "until the session ends or the account is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:278
msgid "WordPress owns this record and removes it with the account. Taking it here would sign the person out of a site they still hold an account on."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:281
msgid "Each passkey enrolled on the account: the name given to the device, when it was added, when it was last used, and the public half of the key."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:282
msgid "A passkey cannot be checked at sign-in without it. Nothing secret is stored: the private half never leaves the device."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:283
msgid "until the passkey is removed, or the account is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:287
msgid "Opt-in recorded changes containing this email address or this account’s numeric reference, and any current site suspension."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:288
msgid "Keeps a reviewed response reversible after activity history expires."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:289
msgid "Until the site owner removes BetterShield with data removal enabled; activity retention does not prune undo records."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:294
msgid "Incident evidence where the account is a recorded actor or subject, with numeric identifiers and event times. No account names or source addresses are copied."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:295
msgid "Preserves the evidence behind an unresolved security investigation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:296
msgid "Open incidents do not expire. Handled incident history follows the site’s retention window."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:298
msgid "Numeric account references and event evidence stay so a security investigation cannot be erased by the account involved."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:301
msgid "The activity rows this account is the actor on: what happened, the name the account had at the time, and the network the request came from."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:302
msgid "It is the record of what happened to the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:305
msgid "The name and the network come off and the rows stay. A security log that can be emptied on request is one an intruder can empty, and the account asking is the account they would be holding."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:308
msgid "Sign-in attempts made under this account’s username: when, how, the outcome, and the network."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:309
msgid "It is what the lockout decision counts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:310
msgid "two days"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:314
msgid "The last username tried from an address that was locked out."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:315
msgid "It is what the lockout screen and the unlock message say the lockout was about."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:316
msgid "until thirty days after the lockout ends"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:318
msgid "A lockout is the record of an address being refused rather than of a person, and clearing it on request would let whoever is locked out end their own lockout."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:321
msgid "Which account an ability was run under, beside the ability’s name and how it ended. What it was asked is stored as a digest and never as itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:322
msgid "An owner has to be able to see what an agent did on their site, and under whose permissions."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:325
msgid "It is the record of what was done to the site through an ability, kept for the reason the activity rows are kept."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:328
msgid "Changes an agent prepared under this account, and changes this account allowed once. The plan is kept as it was read; the confirmation itself is never stored."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:329
msgid "A change made on somebody’s authority has to record whose, and this is that record."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:330
msgid "seven days from the day the change was proposed"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:332
msgid "The proposals keep their plans and lose the people: what was asked for, what was allowed and what became of it stay, and who asked and who allowed comes off. A confirmation with nothing left of it would read as a change nobody ever permitted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:335
msgid "Which administrator minted the credential an assistant reaches this site with, when it was minted, and when it was last used. The credential itself is kept as a digest and the last four characters, and never as itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:336
msgid "Every call an assistant makes runs as that account, so the record of whose permissions apply is the record of what the connection may do."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:337
msgid "until the connection is ended or the credential is replaced"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:339
msgid "It is the record of an assistant being let in, and every call it makes runs as that account. Taking the name off would leave a live connection with nothing saying whose permissions it holds, and removing the connection would cut an assistant off as a side effect of a request that was not about it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:342
msgid "Each application that was allowed to connect: the name it gave, which administrator approved it, when, and when it was last seen. Its tokens are kept as digests and never as themselves."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:343
msgid "An owner has to be able to see which assistants can reach this site and on whose authority, and to cut one off."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:344
msgid "until the application is revoked, or thirty days after it last refreshed its access"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:346
msgid "It is the record of access being granted to something that is not a person. Removing it on request would leave a live connection with nothing saying who allowed it, and the account asking is the account that allowed it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:349
msgid "A mark saying this account has already been told about a sign-in from a network it has not used before."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:350
msgid "One message a day, however many new networks a journey passes through."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:351
msgid "one day"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days the activity log is kept.
#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:363
#, php-format
msgid "%d day from the day it was written"
msgid_plural "%d days from the day it was written"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:479
msgid "This site uses BetterShield to protect and audit itself. It records sign-in attempts and the lockouts that follow repeated failures, keeping the network an attempt came from truncated (the first three groups of an IPv4 address, the first four of an IPv6 one) instead of the address itself, together with the username that was tried."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: how many days activity entries are kept.
#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:484
#, php-format
msgid "It keeps an activity record of what changed on this site and who changed it: the account, the kind of change, and the truncated network. Entries are kept for %d day and removed after that."
msgid_plural "It keeps an activity record of what changed on this site and who changed it: the account, the kind of change, and the truncated network. Entries are kept for %d days and removed after that."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:492
msgid "Where two-factor sign-in or passkeys are in use, it stores what is needed to check them: a shared secret, a passkey’s public credential, and hashes of one-time backup codes. It never stores a password, a session token or a recovery code in a form that can be read back."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:493
msgid "Where an assistant is connected, it records which tool was called and when, with the arguments kept only as a keyed digest rather than as text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:494
msgid "A person can ask for their data through this site’s existing privacy tools: the export includes what BetterShield holds about them, and the erase request removes their name and network from its records while keeping the entries themselves, because a security log is only useful if its entries cannot be removed on request."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:498
msgid "WordPress.org, to read the published checksums for this version of WordPress and of the plugins installed, so files can be compared with the copies their publishers shipped. Nothing about a visitor is sent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:502
msgid "The Pwned Passwords service, only while somebody is choosing a password, and only the first five characters of that password’s hash, which match several hundred published hashes, not one. The comparison happens on this site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:511
msgid "WPDeveloper’s usage service, because this network’s administrator chose to share usage data. At most once a day, and once more if BetterShield is deactivated, it receives a report about the network rather than this site: the network’s address and name, the network administrator’s email address, the WordPress, PHP and web server versions, the plugins installed and which of them are active, and the BetterShield version, with the language and active theme of whichever site sends it. Nothing about visitors or the people who use this site is in it. Privacy policy: https://wpdeveloper.com/privacy-policy"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:512
msgid "WPDeveloper’s usage service, because this site’s owner chose to share usage data. At most once a day, and once more if BetterShield is deactivated, it receives a report with this site’s address and title, the administrator’s email address, the WordPress, PHP and web server versions, the site’s language, the plugins installed and which of them are active, the active theme, and the BetterShield version. Nothing about visitors or the people who use this site is in it. Privacy policy: https://wpdeveloper.com/privacy-policy"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:522
msgid "The AI provider connected to this site under Settings › Connectors, if there is one, and only when somebody managing this site asks for an explanation: of one finding, of the open findings (up to twelve at once), or of an incident. It receives the recorded evidence that explanation is about, with web and email addresses stripped and the accounts and files in an incident named only as placeholders. It never receives file contents, usernames, keys or this site’s address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PersonalData.php:528
msgid "BetterShield Hub, while this site is connected to it. The hub reads this site’s security score and findings and its activity record, which names the account behind each change and the truncated network it came from, and applies or undoes a protection when the site’s owner asks. Privacy policy: https://bettershield.ai/privacy"
msgstr ""

